### LLM Cost Tracker — manual probing (§14.3)
### Use with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or JetBrains HTTP client.
### Start dependencies first:  docker compose up -d
### Then run the Tracker API (profile "http", below) and (optionally) the Admin app.

@tracker = http://localhost:5196
@admin   = http://localhost:5280

### The check/capture endpoints require a valid gateway bearer token (§6.1).
### In local dev the Tracker validates against the configured JWKS/issuer; paste a
### token minted by that issuer here. If GatewayAuth is not configured (no
### JwksEndpoint), auth is disabled and the Authorization header is ignored.
@token = PASTE_GATEWAY_JWT_HERE

### 1) Pre-request budget check (§6.2.1)
POST {{tracker}}/api/budget/check
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "callerId": "alice@example.com",
  "model": "gpt-4o"
}

### 2) Post-response usage capture (§6.2.2)
###    requestId is the idempotency key — repeating the same one does not double-accrue.
POST {{tracker}}/api/usage/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "callerId": "alice@example.com",
  "model": "gpt-4o",
  "tokens": { "input": 1234, "output": 567, "cacheRead": 890, "cacheWrite": 0 },
  "requestId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111"
}

### 3) Localhost-only pricing file import (§8.3) — reachable only from the same machine,
###    no gateway token required. Body is the canonical pricing file (§8.5).
POST {{tracker}}/api/pricing/import
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "generatedAt": "2026-06-25T00:00:00Z",
  "currency": "USD",
  "unit": "per-1M-tokens",
  "providers": [
    {
      "provider": "openai",
      "models": [
        {
          "model": "gpt-4o",
          "fetchedAt": "2026-06-25T00:00:00Z",
          "prices": { "input": 2.50, "output": 10.00, "cacheRead": 1.25, "cacheWrite": null }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

### After issuing check/capture: watch traces & logs in Grafana (http://localhost:3000)
### and Seq (http://localhost:8081), sliced by effective_group / budget_source (§10.2);
### watch spend accrue in the Admin app's Reports view ({{admin}}/reports).
